# Scoped deliberately: only the files where CRLF is *functionally* fatal.
#
# These three carry `#!/usr/bin/env python3` and are documented as directly
# executable on macOS and Linux. A CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an
# interpreter literally named "python3\r", so the script dies with
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" before running a line.
#
# Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true` in its system gitconfig, so a fresh
# Windows clone checks these out with CRLF while `git status` still reports clean
# (the stored blobs stay LF). That broke `mcp-server/tests/test_line_endings.py`
# on an untouched tree during a 2026-09-07 machine bring-up.
#
# Everything else in the repo is intentionally left to the developer's own git
# config — this file is not a repo-wide `* text=auto eol=lf` on purpose.
brain-setup.py          text eol=lf
brain-uninstall.py      text eol=lf
brain_settings_merge.py text eol=lf
